1. View events that an object/class would issue:
>> m = metaclass(matlab.graphics.axis.GeographicAxes)
>>[{m.EventList.Name}; ...
    {m.EventList.ListenAccess}; ...
    arrayfun(@mat2str, [m.EventList.Hidden], 'Uniform',false)]'
	
2. Act when an event has been issued.
>> addlistener(obj, eventName, callbackName);

Note the other syntax for addlistener which triggers a callback function when a property is changed (addlistener(ax,'XLim','PostSet',@cb);) is only applicable for properties whose 'setObservable' attribute is set
to 1. To get a list of such properties for a specific object/class, use the following code:

	meta = metaclass(matlab.graphics.axis.GeographicAxes); % Get the metaclass object
	setObservableProps = {};   % Initialize list for properties
	for prop = meta.PropertyList'
		if prop.SetObservable
			setObservableProps{end+1} = prop.Name;
		end
	end
	setObservableProps = setObservableProps.'


3. Some techniques allowing you to execute a callback function when the user uses scroll to zoom in/out of an axes object:

	3.1:
	for 'regular' axes object (objects of type matlab.graphics.axis.Axes) you can use the following:
		clear;
		fg = figure;
		ax = axes(fg);
		plot(1,1,'ro');

		addlistener(ax,'XLim','PostSet',@cb);
		function cb(metaprop,event)
		% callback code
		disp('');
		end
		
	3.2:
	Another method (which seems to be slower) is to use the parent figure 'WindowScrollWheelFcn' callback. But, defining a function for this callback interferes with
	built in methods of MATLAB when user scrolls. To avoid problems, use the following code:
		clear;
		fg = figure;
		ax = axes(fg);
		plot(1,1,'ro');

		enableDefaultInteractivity(ax) % * <-- must be before assigning ButtonDownFcn
		fg.WindowScrollWheelFcn = @cb;

		function cb(src,event)
		% callback code
		disp('h');
		end
	
	3.3:
	Another generic method is explained in https://undocumentedmatlab.com/articles/undocumented-hg2-graphics-events
	We can use 'MarkedClean' event (which are available for practically all graphic objects) to get a notification whenever the corresponding object is being redrawn.
	The following example uses 'MarkedClean' event of LatitudeAxis subobject of a geoaxes object (which is updated less frequently than the axes itself)
	to execute a callback when use scrolls to zoom in/out. I could not find any better way:
		clear;
		fg = figure;
		gx = geoaxes('Basemap','opentopomap');
		geoscatter(gx,10,10)
		addlistener(gx.LatitudeAxis, 'MarkedClean', @cb);

		function cb(src, event)
		% src
		% event
		disp('h');
		end
	
	
