List all properties of a class along with their access level:
>> m = ?matlab.graphics.chart.StackedLineChart
>> [mat2cell((1:numel(m.PropertyList)).',ones(numel(m.PropertyList),1),1), {m.PropertyList.Name}.', {m.PropertyList.GetAccess}.']

Although you can't retrieve private properties of an object using dot indexing, you can get them using 'struct' technique. 
There is no way you can set private properties (hence private)
Example:
'matlab.graphics.chart.StackedLineChart' object has a private property named 'DataCursor'. To obtain its value you should use the following:
p = struct(plt).DataCursor;

