%%----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Problem:

I have code running in a loop. there is button with its callback defined. when the user presses the button, I want the program to reach the end of the loop before the callback is executed. 
But this is not the behavior of MATLAB. MATLAB interrupts the code and immediately runs the callback.

Solution:
https://www.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/answers/476028-interrupting-a-callback-with-a-push-button#answer_387461

In short, inside the body of the callback function, set a flag variable to true and immediately return from the callback. at the end of the while loop, check
if that flag is true, if it is true, do the job which was intended to be done in the interrupting callback. See script "MotorJoggingGUI_v5.m".

%%----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Problem:

Suppose that you have created a figure with handle `fig` which is invisible (fig.Visible = 'off') and you want to make it the current figure.
the function `figure(fig)` makes the figure the current figure (brings it into focus), BUT it makes it visible. How can I do this without making it visible?

Solution:
>> set(0, 'currentfigure', fig);

